      </memberdef>
      <memberdef kind="function" id="classbs4_1_1dammit_1_1EntitySubstitution_1a731e83a676ce962225705fdfabac2898" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>str</type>
        <definition> str bs4.dammit.EntitySubstitution.substitute_xml</definition>
        <argsstring>(cls, str value, bool make_quoted_attribute=False)</argsstring>
        <name>substitute_xml</name>
        <qualifiedname>bs4.dammit.EntitySubstitution.substitute_xml</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>cls</type>
          <defname>cls</defname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>str</type>
          <declname>value</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>bool</type>
          <declname>make_quoted_attribute</declname>
          <defval>False</defval>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><verbatim>Replace special XML characters with named XML entities.

The less-than sign will become &amp;lt;, the greater-than sign
will become &amp;gt;, and any ampersands will become &amp;amp;. If you
want ampersands that seem to be part of an entity definition
to be left alone, use `substitute_xml_containing_entities`
instead.

:param value: A string to be substituted.

:param make_quoted_attribute: If True, then the string will be
 quoted, as befits an attribute value.

:return: A version of ``value`` with special characters replaced
 with named entities.
